## Table Naming Conventions

### Bronze Rules

- All table names must start with `bronze_<sourcesystem>_` followed by the entity name reflecting the source file/table without business transformations.
- **Pattern:** `bronze_<sourcesystem>_<entity>`
  - `bronze_`: Prefix indicating the Bronze layer.
  - `<sourcesystem>`: Short identifier for the source system (e.g., `ecom` for e-commerce).
  - `<entity>`: Source entity name in `snake_case`.
- **Examples:**
  - `bronze_ecom_product_catalog`
  - `bronze_ecom_customer_master`
  - `bronze_ecom_sales_customer_analytics`
  - `bronze_ecom_order_items`

### Silver Rules

- All table names must start with `silver_<sourcesystem>_` followed by the entity name after data cleansing and type normalization.
- **Pattern:** `silver_<sourcesystem>_<entity>`
- **Examples:**
  - `silver_ecom_product_catalog`
  - `silver_ecom_customer_master`
  - `silver_ecom_orders`
  - `silver_ecom_order_items`

### Gold Rules

- All table names must use business-aligned names starting with an object category prefix.
- **Pattern:** `gold_<category>_<entity>`
  - `<category>`: Indicates the analytical role of the table (`dim`, `fact`, `report`).
  - `<entity>`: Business entity or reporting subject in `snake_case`.

#### Category Prefix Glossary (`Gold`)

| Prefix | Meaning | Examples |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `dim_` | Dimension table (descriptive attributes) | `gold_dim_product`, `gold_dim_customer` |
| `fact_` | Fact table (transactional / measurable events) | `gold_fact_orders`, `gold_fact_order_items` |
| `report_` | Summary or reporting-ready table | `gold_report_sales_monthly`, `gold_report_returns` |

